#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:7
msgid "ament_cmake_python user documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:9
msgid ""
"``ament_cmake_python`` is a package that provides CMake functions for "
"packages of the ``ament_cmake`` build type that contain Python code. See "
"the :doc:`ament_cmake user documentation <Ament-CMake-Documentation>` for "
"more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:14
msgid ""
"Pure Python packages should use the ``ament_python`` build type in most "
"cases. To create an ``ament_python`` package, see :doc:`Creating your first "
"ROS 2 package <../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-"
"Libraries/Creating-Your-First-ROS2-Package>`. ``ament_cmake_python`` should "
"only be used in cases where that is not possible, like when mixing C/C++ and "
"Python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:21
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:24
msgid "Basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:27
msgid "Basic project outline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:29
msgid ""
"The outline of a package called \"my_project\" with the ``ament_cmake`` "
"build type that uses ``ament_cmake_python`` looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:31
msgid ""
".\n"
"└── my_project\n"
"    ├── CMakeLists.txt\n"
"    ├── package.xml\n"
"    └── my_project\n"
"        ├── __init__.py\n"
"        └── my_script.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:41
msgid ""
"The ``__init__.py`` file can be empty, but it is needed to `make Python "
"treat the directory containing it as a package <https://docs.python.org/3/"
"tutorial/modules.html#packages>`__. There can also be a ``src`` or "
"``include`` directory alongside the ``CMakeLists.txt`` which holds C/C++ "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:45
msgid "Using ament_cmake_python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:47
msgid ""
"The package must declare a dependency on ``ament_cmake_python`` in its "
"``package.xml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:49
msgid "<buildtool_depend>ament_cmake_python</buildtool_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:53
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:101
msgid "The ``CMakeLists.txt`` should contain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:55
msgid ""
"find_package(ament_cmake_python REQUIRED)\n"
"# ...\n"
"ament_python_install_package(${PROJECT_NAME})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:61
msgid ""
"The argument to ``ament_python_install_package()`` is the name of the "
"directory alongside the ``CMakeLists.txt`` that contains the Python file. In "
"this case, it is ``my_project``, or ``${PROJECT_NAME}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:66
msgid ""
"Calling ``rosidl_generate_interfaces`` and ``ament_python_install_package`` "
"in the same CMake project does not work. See this `Github issue <https://"
"github.com/ros2/rosidl_python/issues/141>`_ for more info. It is best "
"practice to instead separate out the message generation into a separate "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:70
msgid ""
"Then, another Python package that correctly depends on ``my_project`` can "
"use it as a normal Python module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:72
msgid "from my_project.my_script import my_function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:76
msgid "Assuming ``my_script.py`` contains a function called ``my_function()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:79
msgid "Using ament_cmake_pytest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:81
msgid ""
"The package ``ament_cmake_pytest`` is used to make tests discoverable to "
"``cmake``. The package must declare a test dependency on "
"``ament_cmake_pytest`` in its ``package.xml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:84
msgid "<test_depend>ament_cmake_pytest</test_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:88
msgid ""
"Say the package has a file structure like below, with tests in the ``tests`` "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:90
msgid ""
".\n"
"├── CMakeLists.txt\n"
"├── my_project\n"
"│   └── my_script.py\n"
"├── package.xml\n"
"└── tests\n"
"    ├── test_a.py\n"
"    └── test_b.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:103
msgid ""
"if(BUILD_TESTING)\n"
"  find_package(ament_cmake_pytest REQUIRED)\n"
"  set(_pytest_tests\n"
"    tests/test_a.py\n"
"    tests/test_b.py\n"
"    # Add other test files here\n"
"  )\n"
"  foreach(_test_path ${_pytest_tests})\n"
"    get_filename_component(_test_name ${_test_path} NAME_WE)\n"
"    ament_add_pytest_test(${_test_name} ${_test_path}\n"
"      APPEND_ENV PYTHONPATH=${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}\n"
"      TIMEOUT 60\n"
"      WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}\n"
"    )\n"
"  endforeach()\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:122
msgid ""
"Compared to the usage of ament_python, which supports automatic test "
"discovery, ament_cmake_pytest must be called with the path to each test "
"file. The timeout can be reduced as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Ament-CMake-Python-Documentation.rst:125
msgid ""
"Now, you can invoke your tests with the :doc:`standard colcon testing "
"commands <../Testing/Testing/CLI>`."
msgstr ""
